5. Speech model
---------------
The embedded hold classifier (hold-classifier-accent-r2.onnx) is a modified version
of the Moonshine base speech encoder: its weights were fine-tuned and a new
output layer was added for the dragon-word vocabulary.
Original model: Moonshine base, https://huggingface.co/UsefulSensors/moonshine-base
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2025 Useful Sensors, Inc. (dba Moonshine AI)


6. Model training data
----------------------
No training audio is distributed with thuum. The classifier's fine-tuning used
only synthetic speech and impulse responses/noise from the sources below. No
game audio and no human recordings were used to train it.

Speech synthesisers:
- eSpeak NG (https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng), GPL-3.0-or-later.
  Only its audio output was used; no eSpeak NG code is included.
- Flite (https://github.com/festvox/flite) with the CMU voices slt, rms, awb,
  kal and kal16. Copyright (c) 1999-2017 Language Technologies Institute,
  Carnegie Mellon University; BSD-style license.
- Piper (https://github.com/rhasspy/piper) with these voices from
  https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices, each trained from scratch
  unless noted:
    en_US libritts high - LibriTTS (Zen et al., 2019), CC BY 4.0,
        https://www.openslr.org/60/ ; derived from LibriSpeech (Panayotov et
        al., 2015) and LibriVox recordings
    en_US ljspeech medium - LJ Speech (Keith Ito, 2017), public domain
    en_US kristin, norman and john medium - LibriVox recordings, public
        domain (john fine-tuned from kristin)
    en_GB cori medium - LibriVox recordings, public domain
    no_NO nvcc medium - CC0
    sv_SE nst medium - CC0
    nl_BE rdh medium - CC0
    nl_NL alex medium - CC0, fine-tuned from nl_BE rdh
- VITS (https://github.com/jaywalnut310/vits), MIT, Copyright (c) 2021
  Jaehyeon Kim, with the VCTK checkpoint kakao-enterprise/vits-vctk (MIT),
  trained on the CSTR VCTK Corpus 0.92 (Yamagishi, Veaux, MacDonald,
  University of Edinburgh), CC BY 4.0,
  https://datashare.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/3443

Room impulse responses and noise, from the Room Impulse Response and Noise
Database (OpenSLR SLR28, https://www.openslr.org/28/):
- its simulated room impulse responses, Apache-2.0;
- the Aachen Impulse Response database (RWTH Aachen University), MIT;
- point-source noises from the Freesound portion of MUSAN marked Public
  Domain.


